# Fallback denylist for legacy (non-BuildKit) builders, which ignore the
# per-Dockerfile `crowdsec-abuse-reporter/docker/Dockerfile.dockerignore` allowlist next
# to the Dockerfile. That file is the primary build-context filter under
# BuildKit; this one exists purely as defense in depth so that a
# `DOCKER_BUILDKIT=0 docker build -f crowdsec-abuse-reporter/docker/Dockerfile .` never
# ships secrets, databases, or repo metadata to the daemon.
**/settings.env
**/settings-*.env
**/*.db
**/*.db-*
.git/
**/data/
**/.venv/
**/__pycache__/
**/*.py[cod]
**/.pytest_cache/
**/.ruff_cache/
**/.omc/
**/.claude/
**/BUILD_INFO
**/grafana/
